PART 2: GCD Program

#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int a, b, temp;
    printf("Enter two numbers: ");
    scanf("%d %d", &a, &b);
    while (b != 0) {
        temp = b;
        b = a % b;
        a = temp;
    }
    printf("GCD = %d\n", a);
    return 0;
}

Why goto should be avoided:
1. Makes code unreadable — creates spaghetti code.
2. Breaks structured programming flow.
3. Difficult to debug and maintain.
4. Modern alternatives (break, continue, functions) are cleaner.
5. Can cause infinite loops if used carelessly.

