PART 3: Nested Loop and Series Sum

Nested Loop: A loop placed inside another loop. The inner loop completes all its iterations for each iteration of the outer loop.

Series: 1 + (1+2) + (1+2+3) + ... up to n terms

Term 1: 1 = 1
Term 2: 1+2 = 3
Term 3: 1+2+3 = 6
Total for n=3: 1 + 3 + 6 = 10

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int n, i, j;
    int termSum, totalSum = 0;

    printf("Enter the value of n: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);

    for (i = 1; i <= n; i++) {          // Outer loop: n terms
        termSum = 0;
        for (j = 1; j <= i; j++) {      // Inner loop: sum 1 to i
            termSum += j;
        }
        totalSum += termSum;            // Add term to total
        printf("Term %d = %d\n", i, termSum);
    }

    printf("Sum of series = %d\n", totalSum);
    return 0;
}

Sample Output for n = 4:
Term 1 = 1
Term 2 = 3
Term 3 = 6
Term 4 = 10
Sum of series = 20

PART 1: String Handling Functions in C

All string functions are declared in <string.h>.

1. strlen() — Find String Length:
Returns the number of characters excluding '\0'.
char s[] = "Hello";
printf("%d", strlen(s));  // Output: 5

2. strcpy() — Copy String:
Copies source into destination.
char dest[20], src[] = "World";
strcpy(dest, src);
printf("%s", dest);  // Output: World

3. strcat() — Concatenate Strings:
Appends source to end of destination.
char s1[30] = "Hello ";
strcat(s1, "World");
printf("%s", s1);  // Output: Hello World

4. strcmp() — Compare Strings:
Returns 0 if equal, <0 if s1<s2, >0 if s1>s2.
printf("%d", strcmp("ABC", "ABC"));  // Output: 0
printf("%d", strcmp("ABC", "DEF"));  // Output: negative

5. strrev() — Reverse String:
Reverses the string in place.
char s[] = "Hello";
strrev(s);
printf("%s", s);  // Output: olleH

6. strupr() / strlwr() — Convert Case:
char s1[] = "hello"; strupr(s1); // "HELLO"
char s2[] = "HELLO"; strlwr(s2); // "hello"

---

PART 2: Storage Classes

1. auto: Default for local variables. Scope: block. Lifetime: block. Default: garbage.
void f() { auto int x = 10; }

2. extern: Global variable across files. Scope: program. Lifetime: program. Default: 0.
extern int count;

3. static: Retains value between calls. Scope: local. Lifetime: program. Default: 0.
void f() { static int c = 0; c++; printf("%d ", c); }
// Calls: 1 2 3...

4. register: CPU register storage. Scope: block. Cannot use &.
for (register int i = 0; i < 100; i++) { }

