PART 2: Recursive Sum and Leap Year

Recursive Sum of First 25 Natural Numbers:

#include <stdio.h>

int sumN(int n) {
    if (n == 1)         // Base case
        return 1;
    return n + sumN(n - 1);  // Recursive call
}

int main() {
    int result = sumN(25);
    printf("Sum of first 25 natural numbers = %d\n", result);
    return 0;
}

Output: Sum of first 25 natural numbers = 325
Verification: n(n+1)/2 = 25*26/2 = 325 ✓

Leap Year Program:

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int year;
    printf("Enter a year: ");
    scanf("%d", &year);

    if ((year % 4 == 0 && year % 100 != 0) || (year % 400 == 0))
        printf("%d is a Leap Year\n", year);
    else
        printf("%d is NOT a Leap Year\n", year);

    return 0;
}

Sample Outputs:
Enter a year: 2024 → 2024 is a Leap Year
Enter a year: 1900 → 1900 is NOT a Leap Year
Enter a year: 2000 → 2000 is a Leap Year

